# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MichiKanji — environment variable reference
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development.
# In production (Vercel), add variables via Settings → Environment Variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEND — email delivery
# Required for inquiry form email notifications (Option A).
# Get your API key at https://resend.com → API Keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL — generic webhook notification (Option B, optional)
# Set this to receive a ping in Slack, Discord, Zapier, Make.com, or n8n
# whenever someone submits the /advertise inquiry form.
#
# ⚠️  This is NOT the Resend webhook (/api/webhook/resend).
#     It is a separate HTTP POST endpoint provided by your chat/automation tool.
#
# Examples (replace the angle-bracket placeholders with your actual URL):
#   Slack:    Get URL from your Slack workspace → Apps → Incoming Webhooks
#   Discord:  Server Settings → Integrations → Webhooks → New Webhook → Copy URL
#   Zapier:   Create a "Webhooks by Zapier" Catch Hook trigger and copy the URL
#
# At least one of RESEND_API_KEY or INQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL must be set so that
# inquiry form submissions reach you.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=<paste your webhook URL here>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The weekly-story list (/api/subscribe) — Resend, on our own domain
#
# Kit is gone. We own the whole opt-in: /api/subscribe mints a signed token and
# emails it; /api/subscribe/confirm creates the contact when that token comes
# back. Nothing stores a pending signup — the token IS the pending record.
#
# There is no RESEND_AUDIENCE_ID, and its absence is deliberate. Checked against
# the live dashboard and API reference on 2026-08-25: Resend has ONE Audience per
# account and `audience_id` is gone from the contacts API — the endpoint is a flat
# POST /contacts and contacts are global, keyed by email. What used to be several
# audiences is now Segments and Topics inside the single one. If you find this var
# set anywhere, delete it; nothing reads it.
#
# The signup surface IS now stored in Resend, as the `source` contact property
# (declared in the dashboard under Audience → Properties, string, no fallback,
# created 2026-08-25). It is written by a second, non-fatal call after the contact
# exists — see lib/email/audience.ts. DataFast still records it at capture time via
# trackEmailSignup(source); the difference is that the ESP copy is attached to the
# consent record rather than sitting in analytics.
#
# EMAIL_TOKEN_SECRET — HMAC secret for the 48h confirmation token (HS256).
#   Any long random string: `openssl rand -base64 48`. Rotating it invalidates
#   every confirmation link still in flight, so rotate in a send-free window.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY and EMAIL_TOKEN_SECRET are both required for subscriptions.
# Without either, /api/subscribe answers
# 503 rather than 200 — deliberately, because sendEmail returns a MOCK SUCCESS
# when RESEND_API_KEY is unset (lib/resend.ts), so a missing-config path would
# otherwise tell someone to check an inbox that will never receive anything.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EMAIL_TOKEN_SECRET=
